# Deny everything, then re-include only what the image actually needs.
#
# Inverted deliberately. The previous allow-list-of-exclusions did not mention
# `alertmanager/`, so `alertmanager/slack_url` — a live Slack webhook, gitignored
# precisely because it is a credential — was being copied into every build
# context. It never reached the image, but it did reach the builder and its
# cache, which matters on a shared or remote builder.
#
# With deny-all, a new secret file added to the repo tomorrow is excluded by
# default rather than by someone remembering to come back here.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src
!public

# Re-exclude anything that could reappear inside an allowed tree.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
